{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given `n`, return every string of `n` pairs of parentheses that is **well-formed** — each `)` closes an earlier `(` and every `(` is closed — in any order."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/08a9c0f3-cfa1-4071-a47d-a846cee2bd40.svg",
      "alt": "The tree of choices for n equal to 2, growing one bracket at a time. From the empty start the only allowed move is an opening bracket. From there, either another opening bracket or a closing one. Each branch then has only one allowed move at each step, ending in the two answers, (()) and ()(). No invalid prefix is ever built.",
      "width": 770,
      "height": 556,
      "scene": {
